"""Build and refresh  Block 4\\Deliverables  from the sources of record (manifest-driven, re-runnable).

The Deliverables folder is the one organised place for everything this work produced or relied on: the live report,
the HMS model files, the dam and channel-network tables, shapefiles, KMZ, sediment and climate results, maps, the QGIS
projects, every script, and the references taken from other projects or from the W: server. It is a COPY: the sources
of record stay where they are (W3, Claude Block 04, Hydrology, the server). Nothing is edited here.

    python sync_deliverables.py              copy what is new or changed, rewrite MANIFEST.csv, README.md and SOURCES.md
    python sync_deliverables.py --dry        list what would be copied, copy nothing
    python sync_deliverables.py --check      exit 1 if any copy is stale, missing, or a new source file was never synced
    python sync_deliverables.py --only "05"  limit to the groups whose folder name starts with the text
    python sync_deliverables.py --prune      delete copies the SPEC no longer produces (renamed targets), then sync
    python sync_deliverables.py --new-version   start the next snapshot folder  "<n> Deliverables <ddmmyyyy>"  (Oman date)

Versions: the folder holds numbered snapshots, "1 Deliverables 07102026", "2 Deliverables ...". The sync refreshes the
LATEST snapshot; an older one is frozen the moment the next is created. Stamps are Oman time (UTC+4): the PC clock runs
on US Pacific time. The root QGIS project  Block04_Deliverables.qgz  of a snapshot is generated by build_deliverables_qgis.py.

Rules: only the LIVE report revision is copied (superseded ones stay in W3/report/R#); a single external file above
MAX_COPY_MB is recorded as a pointer, not copied; the HMS DSS result files, the HMS backups and the project 0.5 m DEM
are pointers. Run after every substantive change, like the live documents; --check is the mechanical test.
"""
